  "exploiter_output": {
    "evidence": "Root cause / sink: dolphinscheduler-common/.../LoggerUtils.java:108-111 `readWholeFileContent(String filePath)` \u2014 opens `new FileInputStream(filePath)` on a fully attacker-controlled string with no check that it resolves under the server's log-root directory (trust boundary: any peer able to reach the Netty log-server TCP port, e.g. a compromised/malicious worker or anyone who can hit that port, controls `filePath` end-to-end via JSON-deserialized command fields). Verified in worktree by reading the file directly (see lines above) \u2014 no path normalization, prefix check, or canonicalization exists anywhere between the wire and the FileInputStream/File constructor calls.\n\nThis is one of three sibling sinks fed by the exact same unvalidated-deserialization pattern (JSONUtils.parseObject -> *RequestCommand.getPath() -> LoggerRequestProcessor.process switch) that a complete fix must cover:\n1. VIEW_WHOLE_LOG_REQUEST -> LoggerRequestProcessor.java:86 `LoggerUtils.readWholeFileContent(viewLogRequest.getPath())` -> LoggerUtils.java:108/111 `new FileInputStream(filePath)` (the PoV's target).\n2. GET_LOG_BYTES_REQUEST -> LoggerRequestProcessor.java:79 `getFileContentBytes(getLogRequest.getPath())` -> LoggerRequestProcessor.java:137/138 `new FileInputStream(filePath)`.\n3. ROLL_VIEW_LOG_REQUEST -> LoggerRequestProcessor.java:93 `readPartFileContent(rollViewLogRequest.getPath(), ...)` -> LoggerRequestProcessor.java:160/163-164 `new File(filePath)` + `Files.lines(Paths.get(filePath))`.\n\n(A fourth related sink exists but was out of scope for the alert: REMOVE_TAK_LOG_REQUEST at LoggerRequestProcessor.java:106-112 does `new File(taskLogPath).delete()` on the same kind of unvalidated path \u2014 same root cause, arbitrary file delete instead of read; flagged here for completeness since a patch touching the shared validation helper will likely want to cover it too.)",
    "expected_vulnerable_behavior": "On unpatched code, LoggerRequestProcessor.process() for VIEW_WHOLE_LOG_REQUEST calls LoggerUtils.readWholeFileContent(viewLogRequest.getPath()) with the raw attacker-supplied path, no root confinement or \"..\" rejection. The PoV request path \"<tmp>/logs/../secret/secret.txt\" resolves outside the nominal \"logs\" directory, the FileInputStream opens the secret file, and the response ViewLogResponseCommand.msg contains the unique marker \"DS-POV-SECRET-e598eac7a0c3-4b7e9c\" that was written into a sibling \"secret\" directory never authorized for log access. The JUnit assertion (msg.contains(marker)) passes, so `mvn test -Dtest=PathTraversalPovTest` exits 0.",
    "notes": "Targeted alert trace 1 (VIEW_WHOLE_LOG_REQUEST -> LoggerUtils.readWholeFileContent -> LoggerUtils.java:108/111) as the primary PoV because it is the shortest, cleanest sink (a single-argument FileInputStream open with no surrounding logic) and shares the identical unvalidated-deserialization root cause (JSONUtils.parseObject of a *RequestCommand straight off the Netty wire) with alert traces 2 (GET_LOG_BYTES_REQUEST -> LoggerRequestProcessor.getFileContentBytes) and 3 (ROLL_VIEW_LOG_REQUEST -> LoggerRequestProcessor.readPartFileContent). All three were manually re-verified in the worktree to have zero path validation, so a fix addressing only the traced VIEW_WHOLE_LOG path without a shared/centralized check would leave traces 2 and 3 exploitable \u2014 this is called out explicitly in `evidence` and `regression_hint` for the downstream patcher. The PoV exercises the real, unmodified `LoggerRequestProcessor.process()` and `LoggerUtils.readWholeFileContent()` production code (only the outbound Netty `Channel` is mocked, purely to capture the response); it was verified to exit 0 on the current (vulnerable) tree and to fail (exit 1) when a representative traversal-blocking patch is applied to `LoggerUtils.readWholeFileContent`, then the worktree was restored to its original vulnerable state (`git status --porcelain` shows only the new `.security-pipeline/` directory, no product code modified).",
    "pov_command": "set -e\nSRC=\".security-pipeline/pov/PathTraversalPovTest.java\"\nDEST=\"dolphinscheduler-server/src/test/java/org/apache/dolphinscheduler/server/log/PathTraversalPovTest.java\"\ncp \"$SRC\" \"$DEST\"\ntrap 'rm -f \"$DEST\"' EXIT\nmvn -B -pl dolphinscheduler-server -am test -Dtest=PathTraversalPovTest -DfailIfNoTests=false -Djacoco.skip=true -Dcheckstyle.skip=true",
    "pov_path": ".security-pipeline/pov/PathTraversalPovTest.java",
    "regression_hint": "Invariant a correct fix must enforce: for every path taken from GetLogBytesRequestCommand, ViewLogRequestCommand, and RollViewLogRequestCommand (and ideally RemoveTaskLogRequestCommand), the resolved *canonical* path must lie strictly inside the server's configured task-log root directory (the same root LogUtils.getTaskLogPath()/TaskLogDiscriminator.getLogBase() constructs paths under) before any File/FileInputStream/Files.lines operation is performed. Validation must happen on the canonicalized/normalized path (e.g. File#getCanonicalPath or Path#normalize().toAbsolutePath()), not on the raw string, and must reject the request (throw / return empty / close channel) rather than silently truncating.\n\nKnown bypass variants the fix must also block, not just literal \"..\":\n- Absolute paths that ignore the log root entirely (e.g. \"/etc/passwd\") \u2014 a naive `path.contains(\"..\")` blacklist (as used to validate this PoV) does NOT stop this.\n- Mixed/encoded traversal: \"..%2f\", backslash variants on any platform, doubled slashes, \"./../\", symlink components inside an otherwise-legal subpath.\n- Path built as `logRoot + \"/\" + userSuppliedRelative` where userSuppliedRelative itself contains \"..\" (naive prefix concatenation without normalization still escapes).\n- Any of the three sibling sinks (VIEW_WHOLE_LOG, GET_LOG_BYTES, ROLL_VIEW_LOG) fixed individually while leaving another unpatched \u2014 the fix should centralize the check (e.g. a single `checkPathSecurity`/`isValidLogPath` helper called from all three, and ideally from REMOVE_TAK_LOG_REQUEST too) rather than patching only the traced sink.\n- Fixes that only reject when filePath is non-null/non-empty but skip validation on empty string or null (should fail closed).",
    "status": "pov_created",
    "summary": "Created a JUnit PoV proving CWE-022 arbitrary file read in Apache DolphinScheduler's LoggerRequestProcessor. The processor deserializes an attacker-controlled ViewLogRequestCommand.path off the Netty wire and passes it unvalidated into LoggerUtils.readWholeFileContent(filePath), which opens a FileInputStream directly on that path with zero confinement to a log root. The PoV sends a VIEW_WHOLE_LOG_REQUEST whose path is \"<logsDir>/../secret/secret.txt\" and shows the real (unmocked) production code path returns the contents of a file living outside the intended \"logs\" directory."
  },
